@page "/rules"
@using BlazorAccessibilityToolkit.Rules
<PageTitle>Rule catalog · Blazor Accessibility Toolkit</PageTitle>

<div class="page-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">CI and process</p>
    <h1>Rule catalog</h1>
    <p class="lead">
        Audits combine axe-core 4.14 (WCAG 2.0, 2.1 and 2.2 at levels A and AA by default, best practices on request) with
        the toolkit's own rules below. Rules marked <em>markup</em> run on bUnit markup; <em>browser</em> rules run in the
        live DOM. Every finding carries the WCAG criteria, a remediation, a help link and a fingerprint.
    </p>
</div>

<div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="data">
        <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col">Statuses</th><th scope="col">Fails ShouldHaveNoViolations()</th><th scope="col">Fails the CI gate</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><span class="badge badge--violation">Violation</span> axe-core violations and confident toolkit rules</td><td>yes</td><td>yes</td></tr>
            <tr><td><span class="badge badge--potential">Potential issue</span> heuristics that need context</td><td>with <code>AccessibilityExpectation.Strict</code></td><td>with <code>--fail-on-potential</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><span class="badge badge--inconclusive">Needs review</span> axe-core "incomplete" results</td><td>with <code>Strict</code> or <code>ShouldBeConclusive()</code></td><td>with <code>--fail-on-inconclusive</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><span class="badge badge--manual">Manual review</span> checklist items</td><td>no</td><td>with <code>--fail-on-manual-review</code></td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>

<h2>Toolkit rules (engine blazor-a11y)</h2>
<div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="data rules">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th scope="col">Rule</th>
                <th scope="col">What it checks</th>
                <th scope="col">Status</th>
                <th scope="col">WCAG</th>
                <th scope="col">Runs on</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            @foreach (var rule in ToolkitRules.All)
            {
                <tr>
                    <td><code>@rule.Id</code>@(rule.IsBestPractice ? " (best practice)" : null)</td>
                    <td>@rule.Description</td>
                    <td>@(rule.Status == FindingStatus.Violation ? "Violation" : "Potential issue")</td>
                    <td>@(rule.Wcag.Count == 0 ? "—" : string.Join(", ", rule.Wcag))</td>
                    <td>@string.Join(", ", rule.Environments)</td>
                </tr>
            }
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>
<p>The <code>blazor-markup-*</code> rules are a conservative browserless fallback; they run only when no browser engine is configured, because axe-core covers them.</p>
